# __NAME__

A mySMB marketplace plugin scaffolded by [`create-mysmb-plugin`](https://github.com/mySMB-AI-Studio/mysmb-marketplace).

## Quick start

```
npm install
npm run dev
```

Then open [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173) — that's the **widget harness**. Paste a widget JSON or pick one from the sidebar; it renders live and can call any MCP server you've wired in `plugin/.mcp.json`.

## Build it with Claude

In another terminal, from this folder:

```
claude
```

That starts Claude Code in this project. The `.claude/` folder ships with the skills Claude needs to author widgets, skills, agents, and `$computed` helpers for you. Try:

> "Add a widget that shows my open invoices."
> "Add a skill that creates an invoice."
> "I need a `$computed` that formats Australian phone numbers."

Claude will read the relevant skill, write the file, and tell you to reload the harness.

## What's in here

- **`plugin/`** — the plugin you're building. This is the only folder that ends up in the marketplace.
- **`harness/`** — local-only dev sandbox: a Vite + React widget renderer with an MCP client. Reads `plugin/widgets/*.json` and `plugin/.mcp.json`.
- **`.claude/`** — skills and agents that teach Claude Code how to build mySMB plugins.
- **`CLAUDE.md`** — project orientation that Claude reads on first turn.

## Setting credentials

The harness reads `plugin/.mcp.json` and forwards `${VAR}` placeholders from your shell environment. To set a token before starting:

**macOS / Linux**
```
export __ENV_PREFIX___API_TOKEN=xxx
npm run dev
```

**Windows PowerShell**
```
$env:__ENV_PREFIX___API_TOKEN = "xxx"
npm run dev
```

Every `${VAR}` you reference in `.mcp.json` must also appear in `plugin/README.md` under a `## Configuration` heading, so users (and the validator) know what to set.

## Publishing

When the plugin works the way you want:

1. Copy `plugin/` into the marketplace repo at `mySMB-Plugin-Marketplace/Plugins/plugins/__SLUG__/`.
2. Add an entry to `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`.
3. From the marketplace root: `npx tsx scripts/validate.ts`.
4. Open a PR.

See [CREATING_PLUGINS.md](https://github.com/mySMB-AI-Studio/mysmb-marketplace/blob/main/CREATING_PLUGINS.md) in the marketplace repo for the full reference.
